cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Humanizer: a bilingual interpretable model for repairing AI-drafted academic prose"
message: "If you use the measurements in data/, please cite this repository."
type: software
abstract: >-
  A Claude Code skill that measures how far a passage of academic prose sits from published
  human writing, in Chinese and in English, and prescribes the rewrite. The model is a
  generalised additive model over 45-48 interpretable stylometric features, trained on 200
  matched human/LLM document pairs built from papers published before the release of ChatGPT.
  Includes the measured false-positive rate on held-out published papers, the confounds that
  were controlled rather than exploited, and the full early-stopping record.
keywords:
  - academic writing
  - stylometry
  - AI text detection
  - Chinese academic prose
  - calibration
  - agent skills
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: "2026-08-10"
